# Commit and Push After Code Changes

Railway auto-deploys straight from `main`, and the user wants changes shipped
without having to ask for a commit every time. After making a code change in
this repo (backend or frontend) and verifying it (tests/build/lint as
applicable), commit and push it in the same turn -- don't wait to be asked.

```bash
git add <files>
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
<short summary of the change>

<optional longer explanation -- why, not just what>
EOF
)"
git push
```

- Stage only the files relevant to the change (avoid `git add -A` if there
  are unrelated stray/generated files sitting in the tree).
- Skip auto-committing for purely exploratory/diagnostic one-off scripts the
  user is running locally to debug, or whenever the user explicitly says
  not to commit yet.
